WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:00.960
And now,

00:00:00.960 --> 00:00:03.690
Great Moments in Unintended Consequences.

00:00:03.690 --> 00:00:06.480
Part one: Black Liquor Bonanza.

00:00:06.480 --> 00:00:08.300
The year: 2005.

00:00:08.300 --> 00:00:11.550
The problem: Fossil fuel
consumption is too high

00:00:11.550 --> 00:00:14.530
and biodiesel consumption is too low.

00:00:14.530 --> 00:00:18.100
The solution: Create a generous
tax credit for companies

00:00:18.100 --> 00:00:22.810
who blend fossil fuel with
environmentally-friendly biofuel.

00:00:22.810 --> 00:00:26.220
Sounds like a great idea
with the best of intentions.

00:00:26.220 --> 00:00:28.370
What could possibly go wrong?

00:00:28.370 --> 00:00:32.160
Turns out, paper companies were
already using a pure biofuel

00:00:32.160 --> 00:00:35.260
known as black liquor,
which is extracted from wood

00:00:35.260 --> 00:00:37.530
during the paper-making process.

00:00:37.530 --> 00:00:39.640
It's a super convenient energy source

00:00:39.640 --> 00:00:41.920
to run paper plants and mills.

00:00:41.920 --> 00:00:45.650
But only blended fuels were
eligible for the tax credit,

00:00:45.650 --> 00:00:48.820
so paper companies bought
fossil fuel they didn't need,

00:00:48.820 --> 00:00:51.290
added it to the biofuel
they were already using,

00:00:51.290 --> 00:00:53.940
and instantly qualified for very generous

00:00:53.940 --> 00:00:56.310
blended alternative fuel credits.

00:00:56.310 --> 00:00:59.270
Exactly the opposite of
the tax credit's intent,

00:00:59.270 --> 00:01:02.740
but sometimes it all boils down to paper.

00:01:02.740 --> 00:01:05.250
Part two: Billboard Bans.

00:01:05.250 --> 00:01:07.260
The year: 1968.

00:01:07.260 --> 00:01:09.360
The problem: Billboards cluttering

00:01:09.360 --> 00:01:11.510
the scenic vistas of Vermont.

00:01:11.510 --> 00:01:14.370
The solution: Ban billboards.

00:01:14.370 --> 00:01:17.500
Sounds like a great idea
with the best of intentions.

00:01:17.500 --> 00:01:19.660
What could possibly go wrong?

00:01:19.660 --> 00:01:22.790
As the billboards came down,
something new popped up.

00:01:22.790 --> 00:01:25.260
A 12-foot gorilla holding up a Volkswagen,

00:01:25.260 --> 00:01:27.750
a giant squirrel in a
striped bathing suit,

00:01:27.750 --> 00:01:30.130
a 19-foot genie holding a carpet,

00:01:30.130 --> 00:01:33.740
a veritable zoo of gargantuan
concrete sculptures,

00:01:33.740 --> 00:01:36.420
all in the name of public art.

00:01:36.420 --> 00:01:39.010
It might seem cute until
a development dispute

00:01:39.010 --> 00:01:40.930
with a local bureaucracy results

00:01:40.930 --> 00:01:44.950
in a 700-pound middle
finger on a 16-foot pole.

00:01:44.950 --> 00:01:46.530
Enjoy the view, Vermont.

00:01:46.530 --> 00:01:49.360
Part three: Equal Pay in Colorado.

00:01:49.360 --> 00:01:51.020
The year: 2019.

00:01:51.020 --> 00:01:53.230
The problem: The gender pay gap.

00:01:53.230 --> 00:01:57.290
The solution: The Colorado
Equal Pay for Equal Work Act,

00:01:57.290 --> 00:01:59.570
a bevy of new regulations on employers,

00:01:59.570 --> 00:02:02.340
including a requirement that
all forms of compensation

00:02:02.340 --> 00:02:04.920
be disclosed as part of every job listing

00:02:04.920 --> 00:02:07.130
and a ban on asking job candidates

00:02:07.130 --> 00:02:08.800
about their salary history.

00:02:08.800 --> 00:02:12.010
Sounds like a great idea
with the best of intentions.

00:02:12.010 --> 00:02:14.320
What could possibly go wrong?

00:02:14.320 --> 00:02:16.290
Not only does the law open up companies

00:02:16.290 --> 00:02:19.340
to new legal liabilities
and administrative burdens,

00:02:19.340 --> 00:02:21.690
it also hinders employer flexibility

00:02:21.690 --> 00:02:22.970
when it comes to hiring.

00:02:22.970 --> 00:02:26.290
As a result, some companies
like Samsung, Century 21,

00:02:26.290 --> 00:02:30.930
Cigna, IBM, Nike, even PETA
have simply excluded Colorado

00:02:30.930 --> 00:02:33.420
from their remote job listings.

00:02:33.420 --> 00:02:36.400
Can't have a pay gap if
you don't have a paycheck.

00:02:36.400 --> 00:02:38.420
Mission accomplished, Colorado.

00:02:38.420 --> 00:02:40.920
Great moments in unintended consequences.

00:02:40.920 --> 00:02:43.229
Good intentions, bad results.

